## Workflow (per slice)

1. **Intake** — name the slice, declare which folder it targets, copy the deliverable list above into the slice's working notes.
2. **Gather** — collect input from product owner / stakeholders / tech lead. Plain language. No code, no implementation.
3. **Draft** — write each deliverable file. Skip-with-`N/A` entries get a 2-line file stating the reason.
4. **Peer review** — confirm content is audience-correct (end-user vs BA vs developer), follows folder's content discipline, and every deliverable box is checked.
5. **Publish** — user approval. Update `PRODUCT_BASELINE.md` row for the folder: status `complete` (every box checked, including `N/A`s with reason) or `partial` (some boxes still unchecked — Notes column must name which).

A Product Foundation slice does **not** implement code. Its sole output
is the predefined deliverable files above + the updated row in
`PRODUCT_BASELINE.md`.

## Sprint 0 Exit Gate

Sprint 0 closes — and Sprint 1 may open — **only when**:

- All three slices are at `complete` in `PRODUCT_BASELINE.md` (or explicitly `deferred` per Skip / Defer below with documented fly-blind acknowledgment).
- The first release plan `docs/04-project/releases/v0.1-<slug>.md` exists with sections 1–4 populated.
- The first product wiki build succeeded via `.agent/workflows/build-product-wiki.md` — `dist/wiki/index.html` renders without broken-link errors for filled deliverables.
- Cold-start row 20 returns green.

Developers starting any feature slice in Sprint 1 must be able to answer *"what does this product do, for whom, with what data, on which stack, deployed how?"* from `01/02/03` alone — without asking the user. If they cannot, Sprint 0 has not actually closed.

### ⚠️ MANDATORY: product-foundation-01-product produces roadmap + first release plan

> **This slice has TWO EXTRA MANDATORY OUTPUTS:**
>
> 1. **`docs/01-product/product-roadmap.md`** populated with Vision text
>    **and** ≥1 real row in the Feature Catalog table (each row carrying
>    a `Target Release` cell using semver, e.g. `v0.1-mvp`).
> 2. **`docs/04-project/releases/v0.1-<slug>.md`** created with Sections
>    1–4 filled (Release Goal, Why, Scope, Ship criteria), derived from
>    Feature Catalog rows whose `Wave` is `Foundation`.
>
> **Enforcement (v2.2):** Cold-start row 20 marks `INVALID STATE` and
> blocks all task work if `PRODUCT_BASELINE.md` lists 01-product as
> `complete` while either artifact is missing. The ba-workflow Review
> stage also checks both before allowing Publish.

The product roadmap is the **canonical source** for which features the
product needs. The first release plan turns that catalog into a
deliverable unit. Planner uses both to populate `04-project/backlog.md`
and to commit sprints; AI agent reads them when the user asks
*"what's next?"*. A Sprint 0 that fills `01-product/` but skips either
output leaves AI with no way to sequence future features — and the
mechanical check above will block.

## Skip / Defer

If the user explicitly declines to run a foundation slice (e.g. business
clarity pending stakeholder input):

- Move the commitment row's Status to `deferred`.
- Add a one-line reason in the Status column (e.g. `deferred: pending stakeholder kickoff on YYYY-MM-DD`).
- Leave `PRODUCT_BASELINE.md` status at `not_started` for that folder.
- Every downstream feature slice touching that folder flies blind with acknowledgment.

